   ],
   "tuning": [],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:bad",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Suppose $\\forall 1 \\leq k \\leq R, L_k \\geq 3$. Layer $k$ has $L_k-2$ reasonable and stable experts and $2$ ``bad'' experts ... Top strategy $B$ is reasonable and stable. Then for any arm set, there is an implement of ``bad'' experts s.t. $$R_n^{*} = \\Omega(R \\log n)$$"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Not a minimax lower bound over all algorithms: it holds for structures whose good experts are reasonable and stable, with adversarially designed bad experts. The proof gives (mu_1-mu_K)/(2 kl(mu_K,mu_1)) (R ln n - R^2 ln 4)."
  },
